   "status": "DISAGREE",
   "ruling": "Ruling: ambiguity; amb.2025.mfs_lived_apart_boxes (coordinator decision under the owner's delegation, lane mfs-l1). i1040gi p. 31, Line 6d: \"If you are married filing separately and you lived apart from your spouse for all of 2025, check the box on line 6d. If you don't check the box on line 6d, you may get a math error notice from the IRS.\" The instruction sits under Lines 6a-6d (social security benefits); the project checks the box only on a return with benefits (ssb.has_benefits), the reply on every separate return lived apart all year. Triage d366a5e05a41: 3,175/3,215 agree; the 3 value differences are exactly that case (MFS, apart all year, ssb.has_benefits false: project false, reply true); the other 37 are the reply's unknown status on returns that never answer it (29 incomplete, 8 refused). The chosen reading stands. (carried over from reviews/2025/transcription/f1040.index.json at 870cc146, review of 2026-11-01)",
